# Managed by codex-bridge (copied into the bridge-owned CODEX_HOME on every call).
#
# Codex ships a built-in execpolicy (`default.rules`) that rejects some commands outright,
# e.g. "rm -f style commands are not permitted". The approval gate (gate.py) is the single
# authority for codex-bridge runs, so prefixes the gate already judges are released here.
# Other built-in rejections are still logged to approvals.jsonl as `decided_by: codex_policy`;
# add an override below only after reviewing them.

prefix_rule(pattern = ["rm"], decision = "allow")
